# The framable tool routes, and the only place on this site where
# `frame-ancestors 'none'` does not apply. Owner decision 2026-09-24; business
# rule 33 amended; threat model in `decisions/ADR-019-embed-frame-ancestors.md`.
#
# Read what this rule does NOT change. `connect-src` is still `'none'`, so a
# tool running inside somebody else's page can no more reach the network than
# the same tool on getopentools.com. `script-src` is unchanged. The frame is
# cross-origin, so the embedding page cannot read the text a visitor pastes
# into it, cannot read the output, and cannot restyle or delete the
# attribution link the embed carries.
#
# Two headers here differ from the catch-all and both are required, not
# cosmetic:
#
#   * `X-Frame-Options` is ABSENT, and has to be. It is a legacy header with no
#     value meaning "any origin", and a browser that honours it would block the
#     frame no matter what `frame-ancestors` says. `! X-Frame-Options` unsets
#     the catch-all's `DENY` -- a rule here adds to the earlier rule rather
#     than replacing it, so without the unset line both would ship and DENY
#     would win. `next.config.ts` cannot express an unset at all, which is why
#     its catch-all excludes this prefix by pattern instead.
#   * `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` replaces `same-origin`. A
#     parent page that sets `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` -- any
#     site using SharedArrayBuffer, so most WASM-based ones -- cannot load a
#     `same-origin` subresource from another origin at all.
#
# `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow` is deliberate and is the point of the whole
# programme: the embed copy must never compete in search with the canonical
# tool page it links to, or the embeds would split the ranking signal they
# exist to build. `follow` is what lets the link out of the frame count.
#
# `/embed` itself -- the page that hands a site owner the snippet -- does NOT
# match this rule and keeps `frame-ancestors 'none'`. Only `/embed/<tool>` is
# framable.
/embed/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'none'; font-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors *; img-src 'self' blob: data:; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; webrtc 'block'; worker-src 'self' blob:
  ! X-Frame-Options
  ! Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow
